            1302
          ],
          "block_id": 3,
          "block_order": 4
        },
        {
          "block_label": "formula",
          "block_content": "\\begin{array}{cccc}x_{1}&-2x_{2}&+x_{3}&=0\\\\&x_{2}&-4x_{3}&=4\\\\&-3x_{2}&+13x_{3}&=-9\\\\\\end{array}\\quad 解 \\quad\\begin{bmatrix}1&-2&1&0\\\\0&1&-4&4\\\\0&-3&13&-9\\\\\\end{bmatrix}",
          "block_bbox": [
            273,
            1487,
            3486,
            1899
          ],
          "block_id": 4,
          "block_order": 5
        }
      ],
      "markdown": "$$\\begin{array}{r l r l r l}{x_{1}}&{-2x_{2}}&{+x_{3}}&{=0}\\\\ &{2x_{2}}&{-8x_{3}}&{=8}\\\\ &{-3x_{2}}&{+13x_{3}}&{=-9}\\end{array}\\quad\\begin{array}{r l r l}{\\left[\\begin{matrix}{1}&{-2}&{1}&{0}\\\\ {0}&{2}&{-8}&{8}\\\\ {0}&{-3}&{13}&{-9}\\end{matrix}\\right]}\\end{array}$$\n\nChanging the coefficient of $x_{2}$ from 2 to 1.\n\nThe purpose of this step is to simplify the calculation in the next steps.\n\n\n\n To do it, we multiply the $2^{n d}$ equation by ½2.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{cccc}x_{1}&-2x_{2}&+x_{3}&=0\\\\&x_{2}&-4x_{3}&=4\\\\&-3x_{2}&+13x_{3}&=-9\\\\\\end{array}\\quad 解 \\quad\\begin{bmatrix}1&-2&1&0\\\\0&1&-4&4\\\\0&-3&13&-9\\\\\\end{bmatrix}$$",
